<!--
  Managed-code preservation for the late-bound Meta MRUK camera backend.

  BlackHoleMrukCameraBridge resolves Meta.XR.PassthroughCameraAccess purely by
  name (Type.GetType with an assembly-qualified name, then an AppDomain scan).
  Nothing in this package references MRUK at compile time - that is deliberate,
  so the core Kerr renderer still loads when Meta packages are absent - but it
  also means the managed linker sees no reference and may strip the type or its
  members under IL2CPP with managed stripping enabled.

  Scope of what this actually changes:

  - Windows standalone as currently configured uses Mono2x with managed
    stripping disabled, so this file is a no-op there.
  - The Android/Quest-native player IS configured for IL2CPP, where stripping
    applies. This file is what keeps reflection working in that build.

  `fullname` on <assembly> is the ASSEMBLY name, not the package name; MRUK
  85.0.0 compiles Core/Scripts/PassthroughCameraAccess.cs into
  meta.xr.mrutilitykit. `/` is the nested-type separator, so CameraIntrinsics
  is named as PassthroughCameraAccess/CameraIntrinsics.

  If MRUK is not installed the assembly simply does not resolve; Unity reports
  an unresolved-assembly warning and continues, so this does not reintroduce a
  hard dependency on Meta packages.
-->
<linker>
  <assembly fullname="meta.xr.mrutilitykit">
    <type fullname="Meta.XR.PassthroughCameraAccess" preserve="all" />
    <type fullname="Meta.XR.PassthroughCameraAccess/CameraIntrinsics" preserve="all" />
    <type fullname="Meta.XR.PassthroughCameraAccess/CameraPositionType" preserve="all" />
  </assembly>
</linker>
